<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rss xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" version="2.0"><channel><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link><description>India News Today: Get latest India news and breaking news from India on Times of India. TOI brings the top news headlines from India on Politics, Elections, Current Affairs and more</description><language>en-gb</language><lastBuildDate>2026-10-29T12:50:46+05:30</lastBuildDate><atom:link type="application/rss+xml" rel="self" href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/rssfeeds/-2128936835.cms"/><copyright>Copyright:(C) Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:50:46 IST Bennett Coleman &amp; Co. Ltd, http://in.indiatimes.com/policyterms/1554651.cms</copyright><docs>http://syndication.indiatimes.com/</docs><image><title>India News | Latest India News Today &amp; Real-time News from India, India Breaking News</title><url>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/507610.cms</url><link>https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india</link></image><item><title><![CDATA[Forces fortify key Arunachal bridge to fight dam objectors]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/forces-fortify-key-arunachal-bridge-to-fight-dam-objectors/articleshow/135293686.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135293686.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Protests against the dam at the Dite-Dime bridge have prompted a strong response from law enforcement. The Central Armed Police Forces have been deployed to ensure order in the affected districts. Recent confrontations during a bandh left several people injured, including four women, escalating tensions. As supporters clashed with security, the Dite-Dime bridge emerges as a focal point of strife near the India-China border.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/forces-fortify-key-arunachal-bridge-to-fight-dam-objectors/articleshow/135293686.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/forces-fortify-key-arunachal-bridge-to-fight-dam-objectors/articleshow/135293686.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T12:23:45+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Kangkan Kalita</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135293705,imgsize-1919041.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Cyclone Arnab: Amit Shah speaks to four CMs, says relief operations on 'war footing']]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-arnab-amit-shah-speaks-to-four-cms-says-relief-operations-on-war-footing/articleshow/135292453.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135292453.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Amidst the aftermath of Cyclone Arnab, Union home minister Amit Shah coordinated efforts with chief ministers of the impacted states, pledging essential assistance to alleviate the disaster's effects. With nine fatalities reported in Andhra Pradesh, evacuations were necessary, and significant crop damage affected about 2 lakh hectares. Restoration work is underway, with unwavering support from the central government for the affected regions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-arnab-amit-shah-speaks-to-four-cms-says-relief-operations-on-war-footing/articleshow/135292453.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/cyclone-arnab-amit-shah-speaks-to-four-cms-says-relief-operations-on-war-footing/articleshow/135292453.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T11:56:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Trisha Mahajan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135293425,imgsize-76462.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA['Don't worry about lathis': Rahul calls on people to join INDIA bloc's 'Delhi chalo' march]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-worry-about-lathis-rahul-calls-on-people-to-join-india-blocs-delhi-chalo-march/articleshow/135292996.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/135292996.cms" /&gt;&lt;/a&gt;<![CDATA[Rahul Gandhi invited everyone to partake in the upcoming Chalo Delhi march at Ramlila Maidan. This initiative seeks to challenge purported electoral malfeasance and uphold democratic integrity. He stated the march embodies the nation’s collective desire and is open to all political groups. Student bodies from throughout the political spectrum are encouraged to join. The Congress party plans a significant opposition rally on November 1.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-worry-about-lathis-rahul-calls-on-people-to-join-india-blocs-delhi-chalo-march/articleshow/135292996.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/dont-worry-about-lathis-rahul-calls-on-people-to-join-india-blocs-delhi-chalo-march/articleshow/135292996.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-10-29T11:38:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Rohitashwa Ranjan</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-135293030,imgsize-93886.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[‘Raids to produce reels’: Ex TN CM Stalin cries foul over Vijay govt searching KN Nehru-linked premises]]></title><description>&lt;a href="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/india/raids-to-produce-reels-ex-tn-cm-stalin-cries-foul-over-vijay-govt-searching-kn-nehru-linked-premises/articleshow/135292135.cms"&gt;&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/1